{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head f24f2a8c55314908a36d1875c4f39b102c31732c on branch request/mcp-late-actor-resolution, the implementation of #10952 (an MCP session can address an actor added after the session started), reported by artifacts #11030 (internal/app) and #11031 (cmd/gitseq-mcp) at that head. Independent verification run today in the clean worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/mcp-late-actors; parent is current main 6fad9e8a668d17cf3c35b3f656217deeb97378ee.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md: the application/service layer (internal/app Workspace actor resolution and custody adoption) and the MCP transport/adapter layer (cmd/gitseq-mcp fingerprint/attach/whoami). Custody storage mechanics are unchanged — apphost.LoadConfig is reused read-only; no new persistence path. The diff does not touch docs/reference/architecture.md and does not change any documented contract: the page's custody lock-and-adopt language is honoured (read-only re-read, adoption back into memory under configMu), and the page documents no name-resolution freshness guarantee that this head would alter. No page update needed in this head.\n\nSECURITY. The conditions' four probes all hold. (1) Serialisation of the miss path is real: ResolveActor takes rereadMu, double-checks the in-memory view inside the lock, then re-reads custody once — no retries. Lock order stays rereadMu before configMu and no caller reaches ResolveActor holding configMu or snapshotMu, preserving the documented innermost-lock rule. One honest caveat for the record: rereadMu is package-global rather than per-workspace as the commit wording claims — serialisation holds but coarser; unrelated workspaces contend on misses. Minor, not a defect. (2) TOCTOU: same-process adds already completed before lock acquisition are caught by the in-lock double-check; adds written-but-not-yet-adopted come in with the fresh read. A narrow residual window exists where an add durably